      columns: ["Aspect", "High-yield points"],
      rows: [
        ["Definition", "Pathological discharge = change in **colour, odour, amount or consistency**, or with itch, soreness, dysuria, bleeding or pain; **physiological** discharge is white/clear, non-offensive, cyclical - explain, do not treat."],
        ["Relevant classification", "**Vaginitis** (BV, candida, trichomonas) vs **cervicitis** (chlamydia, gonorrhoea, M. genitalium) vs **PID** - only cervicitis and PID need gonorrhoea-chlamydia cover and partner treatment; NACO **colour-coded kits 1-7**."],
        ["Aetiology & risk factors", "BV: loss of lactobacilli, douching; candida: **diabetes, antibiotics, pregnancy, COC, HIV**; STI/PID: **age under 25, new/multiple partners, partner with discharge**, IUCD insertion (first 20 days), abortion, delivery, instrumentation."],
        ["Pathophysiology", "Oestrogen -> glycogen -> **lactobacilli -> lactic acid pH 3.8-4.5**; loss -> **Gardnerella biofilm (clue cells) -> amines (fishy)**; chlamydia/gonococcus infect **columnar cells** -> ascent past mucus plug -> endometritis -> **salpingitis -> tubal damage (infertility 12/25/50% after 1/2/3 episodes), ectopic**."],
        ["Key history (OPD)", "Colour, consistency, **odour worse after sex/menses (BV)**, **itch (candida)**, pelvic pain, deep dyspareunia, fever, **PCB/IMB**; **LMP - ectopic until excluded**; sexual risk in private; recent instrumentation; diabetes; previous kits; red flags - foul blood-stained discharge over 35 (cancer)."],
        ["Key examination", "Temperature (**over 38.3 C supports PID**), abdomen; speculum with water only - **discharge from walls (vaginitis) or os (cervicitis)**; **mucopurulent friable cervix**; bedside **pH from lateral wall**; whiff test; bimanual - **cervical motion, uterine or adnexal tenderness**."],
        ["Minimal investigations", "**pH, whiff, saline and KOH wet mount**; Gram stain (Nugent); **NAAT for chlamydia/gonorrhoea**; **UPT in pelvic pain**; HIV, syphilis, HBsAg for every STI; PID: CBC, CRP, urine, **TVS if mass/TOA**; glucose and HIV in recurrent candida."],
        ["Diagnostic criteria", "**BV - Amsel 3 of 4**: thin grey discharge, **pH over 4.5**, positive whiff, **clue cells over 20%**; candida - curdy, pH normal, hyphae; trichomonas - frothy green, pH over 4.5, motile trichomonads; **PID (CDC minimum)**: pelvic pain + **any one of CMT, uterine or adnexal tenderness**."],
        ["Treatment - first line", "**BV: metronidazole 400-500 mg BD 7 days** (or gel 0.75% 5 days, clindamycin cream 2% 7 days); **candida: fluconazole 150 mg once** or clotrimazole 500 mg pessary; **trich: metronidazole 500 mg BD 7 days** (women); NACO **Kit 2 (green): secnidazole 2 g + fluconazole 150 mg**."],
        ["Cervicitis & PID", "**Gonorrhoea: ceftriaxone 500 mg IM** (cefixime 400 mg Kit 1); **chlamydia: doxycycline 100 mg BD 7 days** (azithromycin 1 g in pregnancy); **PID outpatient: ceftriaxone 500 mg IM + doxycycline 100 mg BD + metronidazole 500 mg BD x 14 days** (Kit 6 yellow)."],
        ["Escalation / second line", "**Admit PID**: surgical emergency not excluded, **TOA**, pregnancy, severe illness, vomiting, failed oral therapy 72 h -> **ceftriaxone 1 g IV + doxycycline + metronidazole** or clindamycin + gentamicin; **TOA drain if over 7 cm or no response 48-72 h**."],
        ["Partner treatment", "Treat partners for **trichomonas, cervicitis, PID** regardless of symptoms; **not for candida or first-episode BV**; **recurrent symptomatic BV with male partner - consider partner therapy (ACOG 2025)**; abstain until 7 days after both complete treatment."],
        ["Special groups", "**Pregnancy**: topical clotrimazole 7 days (no oral fluconazole), azithromycin for chlamydia, **no doxycycline**, admit PID; **children**: discharge = foreign body or abuse - no speculum; **postmenopausal**: atrophic vaginitis - estriol cream."],
        ["Recurrence", "Recurrent BV (3 or more/year): confirm, **metronidazole gel twice weekly 4-6 months**; recurrent VVC: **fluconazole 150 mg every 72 h x 3 then weekly for 6 months**; check glucose and HIV."],
        ["Complications", "PID: **infertility, ectopic, chronic pelvic pain, TOA, Fitz-Hugh-Curtis perihepatitis**; BV/trich: preterm birth, PID, HIV acquisition."],
        ["Red flags & referral", "Positive UPT with pain/shock (**ectopic**), TOA, no improvement at **72 h**, foul blood-stained discharge over 35 or PCB (biopsy cervix), child with discharge (child protection), non-response to two courses."],
        ["Follow-up & monitoring", "**Review PID at 72 h**; retest chlamydia/gonorrhoea at **3 months**; test of cure in pregnancy; counsel early USG in future pregnancy; IUCD after PID - treat first, insert after 3 months."],
        ["Prevention / programme", "**Four Cs - Compliance, Counselling, Condoms, Contact treatment**; **Suraksha clinics** (NACO) with free kits; chlamydia screening of young women lowers PID; avoid douching."],
        ["Exam one-liners", "**pH over 4.5 = BV or trich**; **clue cells = BV**; strawberry cervix = trich; **one tender sign is enough to treat PID**; do not remove IUCD for PID unless no response 48-72 h."],
      ],
